Without any dust calculation a sender could advertise an \dditional_fee_contribution\ that leaves their change output below the dust threshold.

This checks the post-contribution remainder in \check_fee_output_amount\ against the output's script-aware dust threshold (\Script::minimal_non_dust\, i.e. Core's default dust relay policy via rust-bitcoin — no new policy invented in PDK):

- remainder zero (fully consumed) or >= threshold: contribution stands;
- dust remainder without clamping: new \BuildSenderError::FeeContributionLeavesDustChange\;
- dust remainder with \clamp_fee_contribution\: contribution lowered to leave exactly the threshold (an already-dust output contributes nothing, filtered downstream as before);
- zero contribution: untouched, preserving prior behavior.

Re the scope question on broadcastability checks: this keeps validation to the sender's own advertised values at build time and does not add relay-policy handling elsewhere.

